te with several..."},{"business_id":"wjZwXKDiFBQXlO8-TjQTXA","review_id":"JE16xY3st06CmdZzmQ4hgA","date":"2018-09-04T01:51:04","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9417765140533447,"text_excerpt":"I came here for dinner with 2 friends as we were in town for the week and our tour guide from the free tours by foot Cocktails of the French Quarter recommended this place for dinner. I'm so incredibly glad that we stopped here because the food was so good and the service was amazing. We were in town during Coolinary so there was a special price fixed menu. We all ordered from this menu because when else are we going to get to try this restaurant. Our waiter made sure that our water glasses stayed full. First we got a shot that came with our meal. It was a pineapple based shot that was quite good. Then there was an amazing amuse bouche that was good. However, I wish I had only eaten the t..."},{"business_id":"wjZwXKDiFBQXlO8-TjQTXA","review_id":"DzBHdp8VxClegStoGECtVg","date":"2021-07-13T00:52:16","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9344821572303772,"text_excerpt":"I'll admit, I have my favorite spots that I always hit up when I'm in NOLA. Now, I'm committed to trying at least one new place each time I visit. I'm a bit sad that I never had a meal at Tujague's original location. However, I've had drinks at its historic bar a few times and even had famed mixologist Paul Gustings' improved Grasshopper which is considered the best amongst his peers and I must agree. Supposedly, the drink was invented at Tujague's in 1918 by Philip Guichet. He created it for a cocktail competition in New York where it won 2nd place. Paul put his own unique spin on it when he took over bar duties. (F.Y.I. Paul is no longer at Tujague's.) Founded in 1856 Tujague's (pronoun..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"wjZwXKDiFBQXlO8-TjQTXA","photo_id":"tC-vNZm3QcYktx1JjsNfog","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/tC-vNZm3QcYktx1JjsNfog.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8576551675796509},{"business_id":"wj